        "id": 18338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-06-08T23:46:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm... yeah, it\u0027s good point. The only downside that I see is that we\u0027re possibly authenticating against multiple passwords, as opposed to always having a single active password. But I do like the other benefits, and it eliminates the need for created_at and a default datetime value :) Reworking...",
      "parentUuid": "7aa08908_356f2bfd",
      "revId": "1fd49dbc8620177b0e6798d035319a0163da070b",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7aa08908_d0a99525",
        "filename": "keystone/common/sql/migrate_repo/versions/103_add_new_password_columns.py",
        "patchSetId": 52
      },
      "lineNbr": 27,
